@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ app = Starlette(routes=routes)
 
 Used to add multiple background tasks to a response.
 
-Signature: `BackgroundTasks(tasks=[])`
+Signature: `BackgroundTasks(tasks=None, *, continue_on_error=False)`
 
 ```python
 from starlette.applications import Starlette
@@ -74,5 +74,11 @@ app = Starlette(routes=routes)
 ```
 
 !!! important
-    The tasks are executed in order. In case one of the tasks raises
-    an exception, the following tasks will not get the opportunity to be executed.
+    The tasks are executed in order. By default, if a task raises an exception,
+    the following tasks will not get the opportunity to be executed.
+
+Set `continue_on_error=True` to run all tasks sequentially despite `Exception`
+failures. After all tasks finish, the first exception is re-raised with its
+original callback traceback. `BaseException` failures, including cancellation,
+always propagate immediately and stop the remaining tasks. `continue_on_error`
+must be a boolean; other values raise `ValueError` at construction.
